From: Simon McVittie <smcv@debian.org>
Date: Tue, 4 Dec 2018 23:41:07 +0000
Subject: Reassure compiler that parse_generic_args() always returns a value
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If it isn't told that usage() never returns, gcc 8 warns:

    dbus-proxy.c: In function ‘parse_generic_args’:
    dbus-proxy.c:215:1: warning: control reaches end of non-void function [-Wreturn-type]

Signed-off-by: Simon McVittie <smcv@debian.org>
Applied-upstream: 0.1.1, commit:fbf0208f6e6a4623b8a418bc5b6c96982dc77711
---
 dbus-proxy.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dbus-proxy.c b/dbus-proxy.c
index ce5412f..163df21 100644
--- a/dbus-proxy.c
+++ b/dbus-proxy.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ static const char *argv0;
 static GList *proxies;
 static int sync_fd = -1;
 
+static void usage (int ecode, FILE *out) G_GNUC_NORETURN;
 static void
 usage (int ecode, FILE *out)
 {
